    <string name="about_title">About Piano2MIDI</string>
    <string name="about_text">Converts piano recordings to MIDI using the hFT-Transformer (Hierarchical Frequency-Time Transformer) by Sony, ISMIR 2023 (arXiv:2307.04305).\n\nAll processing happens on this device: audio → 16 kHz log-mel spectrogram → hFT-Transformer → onset/offset/frame/velocity → notes → MIDI.\n\nSource code: MIT License, © Sony Group Corporation.\nModel weights: trained on MAESTRO v3.0.0, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial use only).\n\nOther engines: Basic Pitch © Spotify AB (Apache License 2.0). MT3 code and checkpoints © Google LLC (Apache License 2.0), converted to ONNX and downloaded on demand.\n\nBest results come from solo piano recordings.\n\nThe transcription is split into melody (top line), chords (accompaniment) and bass (lowest line). Tempo, key and chords are detected automatically for the sheet music; adjust the tempo if bars look wrong.\n\nBuilt-in instruments: excerpt of FluidR3_GM by Frank Wen (MIT license). Music font: Bravura by Steinberg (SIL Open Font License).</string>
